Reference-data extracts for the AGS-to-NUTS mapper (harmonization). Each file is a small
row/sheet subset of a much larger published table: same rows and columns as the source, but
xlsx round-tripping through openpyxl can shift numeric cells in their trailing (13th+
significant) digit and can turn an empty-string cell into an absent one; no cell was hand-
typed or otherwise altered in value.

bbsr-ref-kreise-extract.xlsx
Source: BBSR Umsteigeschluessel Kreise, ref-kreise-1990-2024.xlsx, sheets 2013-2014,
2015-2016, 2020-2021 (of 34), rows for Goettingen 03152, Osterode am Harz 03156,
Goettingen (merged) 03159, Cochem-Zell 07135, Mayen-Koblenz 07137, Rhein-Huensrueck-Kreis
07140, Eisenach 16056, Wartburgkreis 16063.
Known upstream defect, reproduced faithfully (not introduced by this extract): sheets
2014-2015 and 2015-2016 carry the 2013-2014 Cochem-Zell to Rhein-Huensrueck split shares
(0.9617 / 0.9828 / 0.9961 and 0.0383 / 0.0172 / 0.0039) on identity rows (07135 to 07135,
07137 to 07137) instead of a transfer row; per-source shares on those two keys do not sum to
1 on this sheet. A re-basing loader must assert per-key share sums and raise, not silently
trust them.
